t":"2020-05-20T08:07:14Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"This message is triggered by the following minimal example:\r\n```python\r\nfrom typing import Any, Type, Union\r\n\r\nPrimitive = Union[Type[str], Type[int], Type[bool], Type[float], Type[None]]  # Unsupported type Type[\"None\"]\r\n\r\n\r\ndef primitive(data: Any, cls: Primitive):\r\n    if cls is type(None):\r\n        return None\r\n    return cls(data) # The line causing the error (if I remove it, the error disappear)\r\n```\r\nI understand that Mypy warns that Type[None] cannot be instantiated. And, the error cannot be silenced with a `# type: ignore` on the concerned line (`return cls(data)`).\r\nIn this example, I can silence it by putting `# type: ignore` on `Primitive` declaration line. However, in my real case, the Primitive type is in a dedicated module, and the issue is even more weird, because the error is then signaled at line *1:1*. And I'm not able to silence it anymore.\r\n\r\nTested with Mypy 0.770 in Python 3.8.","closed_by":{"login":"msullivan","id":340349,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDM0OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/340349?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan","html_url":"https://github.com/msullivan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/msullivan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.c